sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-018-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-018 — Plateau tri-junction (120 degree) claim: Lami balance, periodic froth relaxation, junction-angle statistics — MorphoEval overall 87.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation (overall 87.0/100, up from 40.2/100 in Pass 1; +46.8 points). The remediated script SHA-256-verifies all four vendored specimens, segments the human corneal endothelium (126 cells, 215 vertices), the onion epidermis (47 cells, 68 vertices) and Thompson's own Figs. 103 and 124 (13 and 28 vertices), and scores tri-junction angles with two estimators against a-priori criteria. Every detected vertex in every specimen is three-fold (f3 = 1.000; Plateau's second law). In the isotropic corneal monolayer the chord-angle distribution has median |theta - 120| = 7.2 degrees [bootstrap 95 % CI 6.3, 7.7], SD 12.5 degrees, 81 % within +/-15 degrees, and is statistically indistinguishable from the relaxed equal-tension froth model (two-sample KS D = 0.045, p = 0.60; histogram r = 0.98) while far from the Poisson-Voronoi null (KS D = 0.27; SD 29.5 degrees). The anisotropic onion epidermis and Thompson's Fig. 124 behave as he predicted (still three-fold, angles spread; best-fit anisotropy eps = 0.2 and 0.3), and his Fig. 103 is drawn with median |theta - 120| = 2.3 degrees. Verdict: SUPPORTED. Remaining weaknesses: the branch estimator puts the cornea at 15.9 degrees (estimator sensitivity at the tolerance edge), the onion segmentation under-counts small cells, Fig. 124's four boundary T-junctions are not separated from interior ones, and the model is straight-edged (no film curvature). Overall 87.0/100 (faithfulness 86.3, reproducibility 88.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 18879252d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_018_the_forms_of_tissues_or_cell_a_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-018_the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-aggregates.py at 18879252d, image/png, 1042338 B, 2100×1102 px, artifact_sha256 94aa66cc8749d83f45c1bb611f3f62022d1424a4919ef7c30e670d6d28038347 (sha256 94aa66cc8749d83f45c1bb611f3f62022d1424a4919ef7c30e670d6d28038347), spec_fingerprint b6891b9d48370d1a3d2785b75836612aaca82ba408f906fd75dc438b1a976266. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b6891b9d48370d1a3d2785b75836612aaca82ba408f906fd75dc438b1a976266; artifact_sha256: 94aa66cc8749d83f45c1bb611f3f62022d1424a4919ef7c30e670d6d28038347; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/allium_cepa_epidermis_specimen.jpg=12d2cff76378adae..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/human_corneal_endothelium_specimen.jpg=9daed5fb546e11bf..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/ongrowthform1917thom_0318.jp2=fb329d9ddbe640d8..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/ongrowthform1917thom_0341.jp2=38d6d1a9bc86ad90..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/paper_citations.bib=ef63468ff8403071..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/scout_manifest.json=50b930d12b0f97e0..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/t1917_018_the_forms_of_tissues_or_cell_a_reference.json=213d7c371e7f98fe..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/thompson1917_fig103_maize_parenchyma.png=d1c3c3aa92d21321..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-018/thompson1917_fig124_girardia_epidermis.png=3a33c7b1b82aad70...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-018-the-forms-of-tissues-or-cell-a-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) p. 297: three similar liquid surfaces always meet at 120 degrees; p. 303 Fig. 113 cases (1)-(3): 90 / >90 / 120 degrees as the partition tension t rises to T; pp. 309-310: Lamarle's least-area partition meets in threes at 120 degrees and 'in any ordinary section of a vegetable parenchyma ... cell-walls everywhere meeting, by threes, at angles of 120 degrees, irrespective of the size of the individual cells'. | Thompson (1917) pp. 314, 321-322: epidermal outer walls and growth/traction anisotropy (Fig. 124 Girardia) are stated exceptions where the angles depart from 120 degrees while three-fold meeting persists.; reconstructed_in_script: Lami/Neumann triangle of forces (E1) with the Fig. 113 cases and the inverse map from measured angles to tension ratios; Steiner-vs-cross film lengths (E2); angle-sum identity statistics with vertex-level bootstrap (E3); periodic Poisson-Voronoi vertex network relaxed by analytic-gradient descent with T1 exchanges under E = sum K/2 (A - A0)^2 + Gamma/2 P^2 + sum Lambda(phi) l, Lambda(phi) = Lambda0 (1 + eps cos 2 phi) (E5), in the equal-tension Plateau limit (Gamma = eps = 0), the Farhadifar Case I comparator, and a 7-point eps sweep. | Segmentation of two CC BY-SA micrographs (nucleus-seeded watershed on a Sato ridge image for the corneal endothelium; Sato wall mask -> connected components for the onion epidermis) and skeleton-graph extraction of Thompson's Figs. 103 and 124; tri-cellular junction angles by a chord estimator (straight edges to the neighbouring vertices, primary) and a branch estimator (mean wall offset within R = L_e/3). | Verdict by pre-registered criteria (three-fold fraction >= 0.90 in both micrographs; chord median |theta - 120| <= 15 degrees in the isotropic specimen; dispersion below the Poisson-Voronoi null): SUPPORTED, with the branch-estimator sensitivity (15.9 degrees) reported.; transfer_boundary: 2D en-face projection / plane section of 3D cells; Thompson's 109 deg 28' tetrahedral edge law is not simulated. The vertex model has straight edges, so unlike a real soap froth it cannot realise 120 degrees at every vertex of a disordered tessellation (a straight-sided pentagon's angles sum to 540 degrees); its irreducible chord-angle SD (~10 degrees) is the appropriate null for straight-walled tissue, not an exact 120. | The Commons micrographs are modern specimens not figured by Thompson; because the claim names no species they are specimens of the claim rather than analogues of a named species, and are labelled as modern throughout.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that junction angles are exactly 120 degrees in any tissue, that cortical tensions are measured (they are inferred by inverse Lami only), or anything about the pre-scouted Dryad set doi:10.5061/dryad.mn8cs, which is a DATASET_MISMATCH (Ca2+ ratio imaging with no junction label) and is not used. | Does not model cell division, active junction remodelling, or 3D apico-basal geometry.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Pass 3: add a curved-edge (circular-arc) froth model or a Surface-Evolver-style relaxation so the Plateau limit reaches 120 degrees exactly, and compare specimen tangent angles against it.",
            "remediation needed: Pass 3: digitise a published tricellular-junction angle histogram (e.g. Drosophila notum / wing disc) as an external reference value and add a second, independent assessor.",
            "remediation needed: Pass 3: separate Fig. 124's outer-wall T-junctions from interior vertices (Thompson's p. 314 exemption) and improve the onion pipeline with nucleus markers to recover the small peripheral cells." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.87"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor cloud agent, primary assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

